"""Editorial questions for archaeology and ancient manuscripts."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


ARCHAEOLOGY = """history_origins|How an Archaeological Question Arose|Which observation prompted investigation of one site?|Trace survey records, local knowledge, prior research, and permissions.
famous_examples|A Famous Excavation Reexamined|What does one celebrated site actually establish about past lives?|Compare context, dating, finds, interpretation, and later reassessment.
hidden_stories|People Behind the Excavation|Whose field labor, local knowledge, or descendant perspective is missing from the discovery story?|Use credited records and consented community accounts.
beginner_explainers|Why Context Matters|What changes when an object is recorded in its original layer rather than found without context?|Use one documented find to explain association, dating, and loss of information.
advanced_concepts|Reconstructing Activity from Traces|How can a site plan and residues support more than one account of past use?|Compare stratigraphy, materials, spatial pattern, and experimental tests.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Artifact with Uncertain Function|Which interpretations fit a puzzling find's context and physical traces?|Rank evidence and testable alternatives without sensational leaps.
technology_innovation|A Noninvasive Survey Tool|What did one remote-sensing technique reveal that excavation had not?|Compare resolution, false signals, ground checks, and preservation benefit.
people_personalities|The Excavator's Interpretation|How did a named archaeologist's methods shape one site's story?|Use field notebooks, publication, later critique, and team roles.
major_events|A Discovery Changes a Timeline|Which find revised the date or sequence of one settlement?|Check layer integrity, dating method, and independent confirmation.
how_it_works|From Survey to Curation|How does an archaeological project document, sample, interpret, and care for finds?|Follow one permitted project and its archive.
rise_fall|A Site Interpretation Reconsidered|Which later evidence weakened an early explanation?|Compare original field record, new analysis, and remaining uncertainty.
then_vs_now|One Site Across Excavations|How did later methods or questions change the picture of a previously dug site?|Compare sampled areas, recording standards, and collection access.
future_developments|A Test Without Further Damage|Which question could be answered by reanalyzing curated material or noninvasive survey?|Define predicted evidence, permissions, and conservation limits.
myths_vs_facts|An Ancient-Site Claim Checked|Does a popular claim about one site's age or builders match the evidence?|Read excavation reports, dating records, and community histories.
documentary_stories|A Find's Evidence Trail|How did one object move from discovery through cataloguing and interpretation?|Build a provenance timeline and disclose gaps.
source_trail|Reading an Excavation Report|What did one report record, omit, or infer?|Examine field method, publication date, sampling, and archive availability.
material_evidence|Residue on an Object|What can traces on one artifact reveal about manufacture or use?|Compare lab analysis, contamination control, context, and alternative sources.
chronology_dispute|Dating a Layer|Why do methods give different ages for one deposit?|Compare sample association, calibration, disturbance, and error range.
ordinary_lives|Household Life from Remains|What do structures and discarded materials reveal about daily routines?|Use a bounded assemblage and avoid assigning modern identities without evidence.
power_and_institutions|Who Controlled a Site?|What material evidence supports claims about authority or unequal access?|Compare buildings, distribution, burials, and competing interpretations.
trade_and_exchange|Tracing an Imported Object|How can material sourcing show movement between communities?|Check provenance, dating, trade versus gift, and local copies.
language_and_labels|Naming an Archaeological Culture|Does a research label imply a unified people where evidence is more varied?|Explain original definition, geographic spread, and present community views.
maps_and_borders|A Site in a Past Landscape|How did rivers, routes, and settlement boundaries differ from modern maps?|Use period evidence and paleoenvironmental reconstruction.
conflicting_accounts|Two Readings of One Site|Why do archaeologists disagree about a feature's function?|Compare context, methods, priors, and predictions.
preservation_bias|What the Soil Kept|Which materials and activities are underrepresented at one site?|Assess decay, disturbance, excavation choices, and collection history.
turning_point_test|Was There a Sudden Break?|Does one layer show abrupt change or a longer transition?|Compare multiple dates and material categories across the sequence.
legacy_and_memory|A Site's Living Meaning|How do descendant or local communities relate to an archaeological place?|Use consented voices, management records, and differing perspectives.
field_excavation_context|A Find in Place|What were the layer, association, and recording conditions for one object?|Read plans, photographs, context sheets, and disturbance notes.
field_dating_methods|Independent Dates for a Site|Do two dating methods support the same sequence?|Compare sample selection, calibration, stratigraphy, and uncertainty.
field_artifact_provenance|An Object's Chain of Custody|Can the path from excavation to collection be established?|Check permits, catalogues, transfers, and gaps; avoid legitimizing illicit removal.
field_site_ethics|Who Decides About Excavation?|How do custodians, descendants, researchers, and authorities weigh disturbance?|Review applicable law, consultation, consent, curation, and alternatives.
field_conservation_decision|Preserve In Situ or Remove?|What evidence supports one conservation choice for a vulnerable find?|Compare environmental risk, handling damage, access, and long-term care."""


MANUSCRIPTS = """history_origins|How a Book Tradition Emerged|What evidence shows the early form of one manuscript genre or format?|Compare dated copies, materials, languages, and earlier fragments.
famous_examples|A Famous Manuscript in Detail|What does one celebrated manuscript preserve and what has been lost?|Read catalogue, physical structure, text, repairs, and provenance.
hidden_stories|Scribes and Makers|Whose copying, binding, illumination, or translation work is overlooked?|Use colophons, material analysis, accounts, and cautious attribution.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Manuscript as an Object|How do pages, gatherings, ink, and marginal notes tell its history?|Use a named codex or scroll and distinguish original from later interventions.
advanced_concepts|A Text Across Witnesses|How do variant readings in two manuscripts affect interpretation?|Compare dated witnesses, scribal changes, and editorial choices.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Manuscript Date|Which evidence supports competing dates or origins for one manuscript?|Compare script, material, textual references, and provenance gaps.
technology_innovation|Imaging Recovers a Reading|What did one imaging method reveal about a damaged or overwritten page?|Compare raw images, processing, independent reading, and conservation risk.
people_personalities|A Named Scribe or Owner|Can one person's role in a manuscript's history be established?|Check colophon, inscription, handwriting, and ownership records.
major_events|A Book Survives Dispersal|What event moved or divided one manuscript collection?|Trace inventories, sales, confiscations, transfers, and missing volumes.
how_it_works|Making a Manuscript Book|How did one documented manuscript move from support preparation to writing and binding?|Use material evidence and period records for a named tradition.
rise_fall|A Script Falls Out of Use|Why did one writing style or book form decline?|Compare institutional, material, linguistic, and technological changes.
then_vs_now|A Manuscript Before and After Conservation|What changed in the object and access after treatment?|Compare condition reports, interventions, images, and handling policy.
future_developments|A Better Reading Ahead|Which nondestructive analysis could resolve one textual or material question?|Specify expected signal, uncertainty, permission, and conservation constraints.
myths_vs_facts|A Manuscript Authenticity Claim|Does a claimed date, author, or hidden message match the physical and textual record?|Check catalogue, provenance, script, material, and scholarly alternatives.
documentary_stories|A Manuscript's Journey|How did one book travel from production to present collection?|Build a dated provenance account, making uncertain links visible.
source_trail|Who Catalogued This Book?|How have successive catalogues described one manuscript differently?|Compare date, language expertise, access, and revised identifications.
material_evidence|Ink and Support as Evidence|What can pigment, parchment, palm leaf, or paper analysis reveal?|Compare nondestructive measurements, contamination, and known parallels.
chronology_dispute|Dating Copy and Composition|When was this physical copy made, and when might its text have originated?|Separate material date, script date, colophon claim, and textual history.
ordinary_lives|Readers in the Margins|What do annotations reveal about a manuscript's everyday users?|Read named or dated marginalia without assuming all readers wrote notes.
power_and_institutions|Who Commissioned and Controlled a Book?|How did a court, monastery, school, or household shape one manuscript?|Use patronage marks, inventories, rules, and evidence of actual use.
trade_and_exchange|Materials and Books in Motion|Where did a manuscript's materials and text circulate?|Trace sourcing, copying, translation, and ownership with dated links.
language_and_labels|Naming a Script or Language|Do catalogue labels accurately describe one manuscript's writing?|Compare script, language, dialect, and changing scholarly terms.
maps_and_borders|The Book's Route Across Regions|What can provenance establish about a manuscript's movement?|Map secure locations and distinguish gaps from inferred travel.
conflicting_accounts|Two Readings of a Passage|Why do editors disagree about one difficult word or line?|Compare images, damage, script, variants, and translation assumptions.
preservation_bias|Which Books Survived?|How do climate, reuse, collection, and digitization skew the known corpus?|Compare surviving materials and institutional selection.
turning_point_test|Did a New Script Transform Reading?|What changed in production or access after one writing change?|Compare dated examples, readership evidence, and alternative causes.
legacy_and_memory|A Manuscript in Living Use|How do current communities value a book beyond scholarly content?|Use consented voices, access rules, and custodial priorities.
field_excavation_context|A Manuscript Found in Context|If excavated, what do its layer and associated objects establish?|Check site records, contamination, and custody; do not assume all manuscripts were excavated.
field_dating_methods|Testing a Book's Age|How do radiocarbon, paleography, and internal dates compare?|State what each method dates, sample limits, and uncertainty.
field_urban_life|A Book and City Life|What can one manuscript reveal about work, exchange, or literacy in a named city?|Read the text with genre and audience limits and compare independent records.
field_trade_routes|A Text Along a Route|Which dated copies show a text moving through a trade or pilgrimage network?|Map secure provenance, languages, and copying centers without filling gaps.
field_writing_systems|A Script in Transition|Which letter forms or conventions reveal change in one writing system?|Compare dated samples and distinguish script variation from language change."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("039", "039_archaeology", ARCHAEOLOGY,
                  "Archaeological inference through context, dating, material analysis, provenance, curation, descendant interests, and site stewardship.",
                  "survey and excavation records, context sheets and stratigraphy, laboratory analyses and dating reports, collections catalogues, permits, conservation records, and consented descendant or local accounts",
                  "Protect sites and restricted locations, verify lawful provenance and consultation, distinguish observed context from interpretation, and do not encourage unauthorized digging or collecting.")
    revise_domain("040", "040_ancient_manuscripts_books", MANUSCRIPTS,
                  "Ancient manuscript books as physical objects and textual witnesses through making, copying, language, dating, provenance, conservation, and living use.",
                  "collection catalogues and shelfmarks, high-resolution images, material and conservation reports, dated textual witnesses, colophons, inventories, and custodian accounts",
                  "Distinguish physical copy from text composition, and catalogue claim from verified provenance. Respect custodian access rules and conservation limits; label uncertain readings and translations.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
